        "label": "The three regions",
        "marks": 0,
        "why": "Naming the three regions first fixes where each layer has to be drawn, so the outline comes out in proportion.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Drawing the root as short as the crown. The root is about twice as long.",
          "Leaving out the neck. It is the narrow part held by the gum."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Crown above the gum, neck at the gum, root below it.",
        "margin_note": "A one-line orientation. The marks are in the figure below.",
        "lines": [
          "A tooth has three regions:",
          "1. Crown — the part above the gum.",
          "2. Neck — the narrow part at the gum line.",
          "3. Root — the part fixed in the jaw bone."
